cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Exact expected subgraph counts in the random k-out graph: closed forms, a matched-density Erdős–Rényi contrast, and an orientation invariant"
authors:
  - family-names: Pardeshi
    given-names: Rajveersinh Vishal
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
last-released: 2026-10-18
version: v1.0.0
type: article
abstract: >-
  In the symmetrized random k-out graph each vertex independently selects a
  k-subset of the other n-1 vertices. We give an exact closed formula for the
  expected number of copies of any fixed graph H for all finite (n, k), compute
  triangles, stars and a matched-density Erdős–Rényi contrast exactly, and
  prove a general orientation-invariant constant Omega_k(H) governing all
  fixed-H first moments. Distributional claims beyond two moments are not made.
keywords:
  - random k-out graph
  - subgraph counts
  - triangles
  - clustering
  - stars
  - orientation invariant
  - exact formulae
